+## Request 24: Dashboard (COMPLETED)
+
+### What was done
+- Added dashboard(invoices, asOf) function to src/reports.js:
+  - Analyzes a set of invoices and returns a summary dashboard
+  - Returns { counts, outstanding, overdue, topCustomers }
+  - counts: object with draft, issued, partially_paid, paid counts
+  - outstanding: total amount still due on issued/partially_paid invoices
+  - overdue: { count, amount } from overdueInvoices function
+  - topCustomers: top 3 customers by amount due, as [{ customerId, due }], sorted highest first
+- Updated test/reports.test.js with 21 comprehensive dashboard tests:
+  - Empty and null invoice list handling
+  - Counting invoices by status (all combinations tested)
+  - Calculating outstanding amounts (excludes draft/paid)
+  - Identifying overdue invoices and summing their amounts
+  - Ranking customers by amount due
+  - Limiting topCustomers to 3
+  - Aggregating multiple invoices per customer
+  - Mixed scenarios with all statuses and overdue invoices
+- Test status: All 356 tests passing (including 21 new dashboard tests)
+
+### Design
+- Dashboard provides high-level financial snapshot for reporting
+- Metrics focus on actionable business data: cash flow, overdue risk, customer concentration
+- Non-mutating: takes invoices and asOf date, returns computed summary
+- Integrates cleanly with existing reports.js functions (overdueInvoices, balanceDue)
+- Top customers identified by aggregating across multiple invoices per customer
+- Limited to top 3 for dashboard usability (not overwhelming with data)
+
+### Returned Structure
+```javascript
+{
+  counts: {
+    draft: number,           // invoices not yet issued
+    issued: number,          // issued, awaiting payment
+    partially_paid: number,  // received some payment
+    paid: number            // fully paid
+  },
+  outstanding: number,       // total amount due on issued/partially_paid
+  overdue: {
+    count: number,          // number of invoices past due date
+    amount: number          // total amount overdue
+  },
+  topCustomers: [
+    { customerId: string, due: number },  // top 3 by amount owed
+    // ...
+  ]
+}
+```
+
 ## Next Steps
 - Available for future invoice features (persistence, API endpoints, etc.)
